{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_55dbb060-6d66-4e6e-af9e-e6afa48244d4","role":"user","created":1775378633,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_59b8682cb84b4052a4254134","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"| PDO-1.—Maturity schedules of interest-bearing marketable public debt securities other than regular weekly and 52-week Treasury bills outstanding | 31.0 |\n| PDO-4A.—Al lotments by investor class for marketable public debt securities other than bills | 39.0 |\n| PDO-4B.—Al lotments by investor class for marketable public debt securities, 52-week bills | 41.0 |\n| Al lotments by investor class for marketable public debt securities for bills other than regular weekly securities (historical) | 41.0 |\nTreasury securities (i.e., public debt securities) comprise most of the Federal debt, with securities is sued by other Federal agencies account ing for the rest. Tables in this section of the \"Treasury Bulletin\" reflect the total. Further detailed in for- mation is published in the \"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States.\" Like wise, information on agency securities and on investments of Federal Government accounts in Federal securities is published in the \"Monthly Treasury Statement of Receipts and Out lays of the United States Government.\"\n| End of fis cal year or month > End of fis cal year or month | Amount outstanding > Total (1) | Amount outstanding > Public debt securities (2) | Amount outstanding > Agency securities (3) | Government accounts > Total (4) | Government accounts > Public debt securities (5) | Government accounts > Agency securities (6) | The public > Total (7) | The public > Public debt securities (8) | The public > Agency securities (9) |\nTable PDO-1 provides a maturity schedule of interest-bearing marketable public debt securities other than regular weekly and 52-week bills. All unmatured Treasury notes and bonds are listed in maturity order, from earliest to latest. A separate breakout is provided for the combined holdings of the Government accounts and Federal Reserve Banks (FRBs), so that the \"all other investors\" category includes all private holdings.\nTA BLEPDO-1.—Maturity Schedules of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, June 30, 2000\nTA BLEPDO-1.—Maturity Schedules of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, June 30, 2000, con.\nTA BLEPDO-1.—Maturity Schedules of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, June 30, 2000, con.\nTA BLEPDO-1.—Maturity Schedules of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, June 30, 2000, con.\nTABLEPDO-1.—Maturity Schedules of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, June 30, 2000, con.\nTABLE PDO-4A.—Allotments by Investor Class for Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Bills\nTABLE PDO-4A.—Allotments by Investor Class for Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Bills, con.\nTABLE PDO-4B.—Allotments by Investor Class for Marketable Public Debt Securities, 52-Week Bills\nTABLE PDO-4B.—All lot ments by Investor Class for Marketable Public Debt Securities for Bills Other than Regular Weekly Series (Historical)**\nFederal securities presented in the following tables are public debt securities such as savings bonds, bills, notes and bonds that the Treasury issues. The tables also detail debt issued by other Federal agencies under special financing authorities. [See the Federal debt (FD) tables for a more complete description of the Federal debt.]\nTable OFS-2 presents the estimated amount of public debt securities held by private investors. Information is obtained from sources such as the Federal financial i