{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775378646-wWxYIQmSRXmxP0vId2ri","role":"assistant","created":1775378656,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to calculate the Debt Sustainability Indicator (DSI) which is defined as \"the coefficient of variation of year-to-year log growth rates\".\n\nFor the fiscal years 1995-1999, I need:\n1. Public debt securities held by U.S. government accounts (column 5)\n2. Public debt securities held by the public (column 8)\n\nFrom the data in table FD-1:\n- 1995: Gov = 1,320,784; Public = 3,653,199\n- 1996: Gov = 1,447,001; Public = 3,777,810\n- 1997: Gov = 1,598,459; Public = 3,814,687\n- 1998: Gov = 1,765,580; Public = 3,760,613\n- 1999: Gov = 1,989,072; Public = 3,667,199\n\nThe year-to-year log growth rates are:\n- For 1996: ln(1996 value / 1995 value)\n- For 1997: ln(1997 value / 1996 value)\n- For 1998: ln(1998 value / 1997 value)\n- For 1999: ln(1999 value / 1998 value)\n\nThat's 4 log growth rates (1996-1995, 1997-1996, 1998-1997, 1999-1998).\n\nThen for each series, I calculate:\n- Mean of the 4 log growth rates\n- Population standard deviation of the 4 log growth rates\n- Coefficient of variation = population std dev / |mean|\n\nLet me do this calculation.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_51b9ebd9bedb42068228323d","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Data from FD-1 table (in millions of dollars)\n# Public debt securities held by U.S. Government accounts (column 5)\ngov_accounts = {\n    1995: 1320784,\n    1996: 1447001,\n    1997: 1598459,\n    1998: 1765580,\n    1999: 1989072\n}\n\n# Public debt securities held by the public (column 8)\npublic_holdings = {\n    1995: 3653199,\n    1996: 3777810,\n    1997: 3814687,\n    1998: 3760613,\n    1999: 3667199\n}\n\n# Calculate year-to-year log growth rates\n# Log growth rate = ln(value_t / value_{t-1})\n\ndef calc_log_growth_rates(data):\n    years = sorted(data.keys())\n    log_growth_rates = []\n    for i in range(1, len(years)):\n        prev_year = years[i-1]\n        curr_year = years[i]\n        growth_rate = math.log(data[curr_year] / data[prev_year])\n        log_growth_rates.append(growth_rate)\n        print(f\"Log growth rate {curr_year}/{prev_year}: {growth_rate:.10f}\")\n    return log_growth_rates\n\nprint(\"=== Public debt securities held by U.S. Government accounts ===\")\ngov_growth_rates = calc_log_growth_rates(gov_accounts)\nprint(f\"\\nLog growth rates: {gov_growth_rates}\")\nprint(f\"Mean: {np.mean(gov_growth_rates):.10f}\")\nprint(f\"Population std dev: {np.std(gov_growth_rates, ddof=0):.10f}\")\ngov_mean = np.mean(gov_growth_rates)\ngov_std = np.std(gov_growth_rates, ddof=0)\ngov_cv = gov_std / abs(gov_mean)\nprint(f\"Coefficient of variation (DSI for Gov accounts): {gov_cv:.10f}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== Public debt securities held by the public ===\")\npublic_growth_rates = calc_log_growth_rates(public_holdings)\nprint(f\"\\nLog growth rates: {public_growth_rates}\")\nprint(f\"Mean: {np.mean(public_growth_rates):.10f}\")\nprint(f\"Population std dev: {np.std(public_growth_rates, ddof=0):.10f}\")\npublic_mean = np.mean(public_growth_rates)\npublic_std = np.std(public_growth_rates, ddof=0)\npublic_cv = public_std / abs(public_mean)\nprint(f\"Coefficient of variation (DSI for Public): {public_cv:.10f}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== Absolute Difference ===\")\nabs_diff = abs(gov_cv - public_cv)\nprint(f\"Absolute difference: {abs_diff:.10f}\")\nprint(f\"Absolute difference (rounded to 3 decimal places): {round(abs_diff, 3)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
